{"id": "X-GAP-003", "verdict": "corrected", "corrected_text": "A pending token produced by decode is a TokenData holding only its id (the executor looks up embeddings only for a prefill's last token and, in GetTokenToDecode, for the token about to be decoded), and FillInputBufferWithToken writes a token without embedding as its int32 id in the first 4 bytes of the input and zeros after it. In our build, PrefillInternal first looks up the embeddings and per-layer embeddings of a pending token that has none (LookupPendingTokenEmbeddings; ours: a82611eb), so for the Gemma 4 E2B/E4B files, whose prefill signatures take embeddings and per-layer embeddings rather than token ids, the stop token that the next prefill writes first gets its own embedding. In the release Agello ships it gets the id-and-zeros row in both inputs instead, so its KV entry is not computed from '<turn|>'.", "corrected_sources": [{"type": "code", "repo": "litert-lm", "sha": "b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7", "pin": "b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7", "path": "runtime/executor/llm_litert_compiled_model_executor.cc", "lines": [1611, 1632], "symbol": null, "lines_sha1": "7f0c11965198f19f5429fb2c85f44f6f897ec118", "url": "https://github.com/PowerBeef/agello-litert-lm/blob/b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7/runtime/executor/llm_litert_compiled_model_executor.cc#L1611-L1632"}, {"type": "code", "repo": "litert-lm", "sha": "b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7", "pin": "b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7", "path": "runtime/executor/llm_litert_compiled_model_executor.cc", "lines": [876, 929], "symbol": null, "lines_sha1": "e1939374c2675b34a31a14842917021dc5bd2ab1", "url": "https://github.com/PowerBeef/agello-litert-lm/blob/b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7/runtime/executor/llm_litert_compiled_model_executor.cc#L876-L929"}, {"type": "code", "repo": "litert-lm", "sha": "b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7", "pin": "b7b856a0cf7e2304f556e985218bc698768233f7", "path": "